      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bedford Charter Township, first organized in 1839, began as Milton Township and held its inaugural town meeting on April 1, 1838.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedford_Charter_Township%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The township adopted charter status to shield itself from annexation by the nearby city of Battle Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedford_Charter_Township%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Harmonia Cemetery, listed as site L1131A on the State Historical list, was registered on November 30, 1982.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bedford_Charter_Township%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fire Station 3 opened on Morgan Road in 1960, and a modern facility built in 2002 now houses the township’s offices.",
